  "question": {
    "text": "Two radioactive substances <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> have decay constants <math><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></math> respectively. At<math><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, a sample has the same number of the two nuclei. The time taken for the ratio of the number of nuclei to become <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> will be"
